sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch03-18> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In plaice of fixed length, weight falls from about November to March or April and is restored between May or June and November, a periodic change caused wholly by spawning and the subsequent rebuilding of tissues and gonads, so that the spawning season can be determined from length and weight alone.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Seasonal cycle in fish weight at fixed length is caused by spawning";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter III, “The Rate of Growth”; topic “Weight-length coefficient in fish”. Scope: plaice and similar seasonally spawning fishes"
}
